@@name
docs
@@description
Make the documentation or text change described in the user request, accurately and in the existing style.
@@requirements
    - Match the tone, formatting and terminology already used in the document
    - Every command, path, flag or code sample you touch is correct for the current code
    - Links and cross-references you add or change resolve
@@approach
    Before editing, reason through:
    - Which files contain the text in question (there may be copies, e.g. README and docs site)
    - Whether the change needs to be mirrored elsewhere
    Commit to the full set of files and edit them together.
@@verification
    - Re-read the rendered or raw changed text and confirm it reads correctly in context
@@constraints
    - Change only the text the request is about; no unrelated rewording
    - Documentation-only: no code changes
@@out-of-scope
    - Restructuring or restyling whole documents
